<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Connections on YoSQL</title><link>https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/tags/connections/</link><description>Recent content in Connections on YoSQL</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/tags/connections/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Transactions</title><link>https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/sql/transactions/</link><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/sql/transactions/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;YoSQL&lt;/code&gt; generates no transaction management, opens no transaction of its own, and has no opinion
about where yours come from. What it generates is the one thing a transaction needs: every statement
is reachable on a connection you supply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="two-shapes-for-every-statement"&gt;Two shapes for every statement&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each statement generates two methods with the same name:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-java" data-lang="java"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Tenant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findTenant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Tenant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findTenant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first takes a connection from the repository&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;DataSource&lt;/code&gt; and closes it. The second runs on
the connection it is given and leaves it open, so several statements can share one — which is all a
transaction is.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>